# LAB4a3: id's 72 fps cap on a 240 Hz screen, at quarter speed, against a frame every
# refresh. Left (A) `clock id`, id's frame gate (Host_FilterTime), passes every 4th
# refresh, so the screen holds each picture for 4 (three refreshes are 12.5 ms, under its
# 1/72 s less its 1 ms tolerance: 60 game frames a second; AUDIT.md, "Host loop"); right
# (B) `clock free`, a frame every refresh. A run down e1m1's first corridor at about 137
# units a second, swaying 8 degrees either way every 2.6 s, id's bob; the Classic box with
# the status bar, the gun and settings 1 to 3; the keys at 4 times their times: `speed
# 0.25` in a 60 fps film is a 240 Hz refresh every film frame. The window is the run's
# game seconds 2.75 to 4.875 (film frames 660..1170, 8.5 s): 1.625 s of run with 0.25 s
# handles. The sound is B's on the game's clock, slowed with it (`sound game`). Render the
# window from its own first frame: the screen's refreshes are counted from there.
#
# Under V3-30: "id capped the game at seventy-two frames a second, and tuned it there."
#
# Assembly (LAB4a): the tool's own split, A's left half and B's right; the edit centres
# the 1440x1080 frame on a black 1920x1080 one and lays its labels over it.

map e1m1

duration 34
fps 60
size 1440x1080
frames 660..1170

preset classic
mode 960x600
display 4:3 240
speed 0.25
hud on
gun on
bob on
player camera
cvar gamma 0.8
cvar r_torchflicker 1
cvar r_lerplightstyles 1
cvar r_lerpmove 1
cvar r_lerpmodels 1

ab clock id | clock free
split line
absound b

camera path
key 0.0000  480,-352.000,110  0,90.000  ease linear
key 0.1333  480,-352.000,110  0,90.000  ease linear
key 0.2667  480,-352.000,110  0,90.000  ease linear
